This function must sort the list given as a parameter, using the function pointer cmp to select the order to apply, and returns a pointer to the first element of the sorted list.

Duplications must remain.

Inputs will always be consistent.

Functions passed as cmp will always return a value different from 0 if a and b are in the right order, 0 otherwise. For example, the following function used as cmp will sort the list in ascending order:

